      en: "The Round Castle of Mardakan, also called the Small Mardakan Tower, is a 13th-century defensive tower on the Absheron Peninsula. Constructed from local limestone, it stands 12.5 meters tall with a diameter of 10.2 meters and walls up to 2.3 meters thick. The tower served as a watchtower and signal post to alert against invasions from the Caspian Sea. It is part of the Mardakan castle complex, which includes the quadrangular castle. Designated a historical monument, it provides insight into medieval Azerbaijani military architecture and is a popular site for tourists interested in the region's history.",
