      en: "Shaghan Castle is a medieval fortress in the village of Shaghan on the Absheron Peninsula, about 30 km northeast of Baku. Dating from the 12th to 14th centuries, it features a rectangular layout with corner towers. The walls, built of dressed limestone, reach a height of 7 meters. The castle served to protect trade routes and includes cisterns for water storage. Partially restored in the 19th century, it retains its original character. Though less known than other castles, it offers a glimpse into medieval Azerbaijani fortifications.",
